The program of omp-target-allocate.m, compiled by the driver for the
machine's GPU and run there: its 3.2 MB of cells need LLVM libc's GPU
allocator, which the OpenMP device runtime's malloc is when it is built
with libc for the GPU.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/omp-target-allocate.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY %t \
RUN:   | FileCheck %S/omp-target-allocate.m --check-prefix=OUTPUT --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
